  "question": {
    "text": "Two beams of red and violet colours are made to pass separately through a prism (angle of the prism is $60^{\\circ}$ ). In the position of minimum deviation, the angle of refraction will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jOy8e",
      "text": "\n$30^{\\circ}$ for both the colours\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "seD2y",
      "text": "\ngreater for the violet colour\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dTavG",
      "text": "\ngreater for the red colour\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "p14Z1",
      "text": "\nequal but not $30^{\\circ}$ for both the colours",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "At minimum deviation $\\left(\\delta=\\delta_m\\right)$ :\n$$\nr_1=r_2=\\frac{A}{2}=\\frac{60^{\\circ}}{2}=30^{\\circ}\n$$\n(For both colours)\n$\\therefore$ correct answer is (a).",
    "image": null
  },
